 * {{Symbol|Projectile|Ripple}} {{to}} [[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Visualized icon-1.png|105px]][[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Visualized icon-2.png|105px]][[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Visualized icon-3.png|105px]] {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}}
** Can affect enemy units up to {{Symbol|bonus cas}} {{Symbol|bonus aoe}} {{#expr:{{#var:Shockwave value3}}+{{#var:Shockwave value2}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus t4r}} {{ValueColor||{{#expr:{{#var:Shockwave value3}}+{{#var:Shockwave value2 tal}}}}|25tal}})-distance away with the wave distance and radius.
** {{hi|Magnus}} {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}} [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|P|21px]] {{Symbol|Target|Area}} ... {{Symbol|Target|Area}} [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|Q|21px]]
*** Creates {{Symbol|bonus cas}} {{#expr:ceil({{#var:Shockwave value2}}/(trunc({{#var:Shockwave value2}}/(30*{{#var:Shockwave value2}}-6000)*{{#var:Shockwave value4}})))}} ({{Symbol|bonus t4r}} {{ValueColor||{{#expr:ceil({{#var:Shockwave value2 tal}}/(trunc({{#var:Shockwave value2 tal}}/(30*{{#var:Shockwave value2 tal}}-6000)*{{#var:Shockwave value4}})))}}|25tal}}) ({{Code|n}}) wave radii that advances forward in {{#var:Shockwave value4}}-{{M|projectile speed|text=speed}} ({{Code|s}}) according to Magnus' [[facing angle]], and takes {{#expr:{{#var:Shockwave value2}}/{{#var:Shockwave value4}} round2}} ({{Symbol|bonus t4r}} {{ValueColor||{{#expr:{{#var:Shockwave value2 tal}}/{{#var:Shockwave value4}} round2}}|25tal}}) seconds to reach max distance ({{Code|d}}).
**** The first {{Symbol|Target|Area-Dummy}} wave radius is placed {{calc|trunc(v1/(30*v1-6000)*{{#var:Shockwave value4}})|v1={{#var:Shockwave value2}}}}-distance in front of Magnus, point [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|O|21px]] , subsequent [[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Wave Radius icon.png|42px]] wave radii [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|P|21px]] are spaced at the same distance evenly apart while the {{M|projectile}} advances to {{Code|d}}.
**** The distance between each wave radius ({{Code|r}}) is defined as:
***** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|r {{=}} d / (30d - 6000) × s}}
***** Hence, if {{Code|r}} has a [[Wikipedia:Remainder|remainder]] value, the position of the last wave radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|Q|21px]] will be slightly closer to the second last wave radius ({{Code|P<sub>n-1</sub>}}) to ensure that the max wave distance remains the same.

* {{Symbol|Forced Movement}}
** The direction of the [[knockback]]-based pull points toward the center of each wave radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|P|21px]] and its trajectory.
** After being pulled, the debuff-affected enemy unit will be closer to the centerline of the {{Symbol|Target|Point}} {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} point-targeted cast location.
*** Hence, the further the distance the debuff-affected enemy units are from the center, the potent the pull toward the Shockwave's center, compared to the pull applied to the point-targeted cast location.
** {{Symbol|Projectile|Ripple}}
*** As the {{M|projectile}} advances, each wave radius sequentially performs a check for valid enemy units within its radius, following its traveling direction.
*** The ability effects are applied as follows:
***# {{Symbol|Forced Movement}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|magnataur_shockwave_pull}}
***#* {{Symbol|Trees}}
***#** [[Trees]] that enemy units come into contact with are destroyed.
***# {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|magnataur_shockwave}}
***#* Reapplying the {{M|movement speed}} slow debuff refreshes its duration.
***# The {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}}.

* {{cf|talnotes}}
** [[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Visualized icon-1.png|105px]][[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Visualized icon-2.png|105px]][[File:Dota2 Magnus Shockwave Visualized icon-3.png|105px]] {{Symbol|Facing Angle|l}}
*** Unlike the primary shockwave, the secondary Shockwaves pulls affected enemy units in the opposite direction of the trajectory centers, and pushes them away from each wave radius' centerpoint.
**** Hence, after the secondary pull, targets will be moved further away from the centerline of the casting direction.
*** {{hi|Magnus}} {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}} [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|P|21px]] {{Symbol|Target|Area}} ... {{Symbol|Target|Area}} [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|Q|21px]]
**** Utilizes the same set of wave radius as the original shockwave.
**** The pull checks begin at the last wave radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|Q|21px]] , then proceed in reverse order, moving back toward the wave radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|P|21px]] nearest to the Magnus.
***** Hence, when Magnus affected by {{M|forced movement}} sources, it returns to the Magnus' current position.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Shockwave icon0}}
| desc = Magnus sends out a wave of force, damaging enemy units in a line, pulling them towards him, and slowing them for a brief period.
}}
* {{Symbol|fx|s}} {{Symbol|fx|v}}
** All ability effects are audio and visible upon its {{M|cast point}}.

* {{Symbol|Target|Point}} {{Symbol|Target|Unit}}
** Both point-targeted and unit-targeted have no difference functionality-wise.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}} {{Symbol|Forced Movement}}
** Affected units are knocked {{#var:Shockwave value6}}-distance over {{#var:Shockwave value7}} seconds at {{#expr:{{#var:Shockwave value6}}/{{#var:Shockwave value7}}}}-speed.

